<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Manuel Enrique Araujo</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1865">1865</a>–<a href="/years/1913">1913</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Manuel Enrique Araujo was a Salvadoran physician and president from 1911 to 1913. His government founded the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/national-guard-dominican-republic">National Guard</a>, a rural police force, and was remembered for its relative tolerance and reforms. He was attacked with machetes in a park in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/san-salvador">San Salvador</a> in February 1913 and died of his wounds days later, opening the way for the Meléndez family's rule.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/manuel-enrique-araujo.jpg" alt="Manuel Enrique Araujo" width="320" height="428" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: George Grantham Bain Collection (Library of Congress) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Manuel_Enrique_Araujo_01.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
